{"title":"Why plants need sunlight to make food","key_idea":"Plants use sunlight along with water and carbon dioxide to make glucose (food) and release oxygen, so without sunlight they cannot survive.","method":["Identify the three things a plant takes in: sunlight from above, water through the roots, and carbon dioxide from the air around the leaves.","Remember that the plant uses these three ingredients together to make glucose, which is the food that keeps the plant alive and healthy.","Understand that without any one ingredient — especially sunlight — the plant cannot complete this process and will gradually weaken and die."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A plant is placed indoors away from any window. What will happen to it after several weeks?","steps":["The plant cannot receive sunlight because it is inside away from light.","Without sunlight, even though water and air are available, the plant cannot make glucose.","The plant uses up its stored food but cannot make new food, so it becomes weak.","After several weeks, the plant will turn pale, stop growing, and may die."],"answer":"The plant will gradually turn pale, stop growing, and die because it cannot make food without sunlight."},"key_terms":[{"term":"photosynthesis","meaning":"the process where plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make food and oxygen"},{"term":"glucose","meaning":"the sugar food that plants make and use to grow and stay healthy"},{"term":"carbon dioxide","meaning":"a gas in the air that plants take in through tiny holes in their leaves"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking that plants get all their food from the soil — they actually make their own food using sunlight.","Forgetting that sunlight is as important as water; without light, the other ingredients alone cannot help the plant."],"remember":"Sunlight, water, and air are the three essential ingredients; without sunlight, a plant cannot make its own food.","quick_check":[{"q":"If a plant gets plenty of water and air but is kept in complete darkness, why will it still die?","a":"Because without sunlight, it cannot make glucose (food) to stay alive, even though it has the other two ingredients."},{"q":"Name the gas that plants take from the air during photosynthesis.","a":"Carbon dioxide."}],"tell_your_child":"Think of photosynthesis like a plant's kitchen: sunlight is the heat, water is one ingredient, and air provides another ingredient, so the plant can cook its own food. If you switch off the heat (no sunlight), the plant cannot cook anything and will get weaker and weaker."}
```
